  "openSystemSettings": "Open system settings",
  "refreshStatus": "Refresh status",
  "permissionsRevokeHint": "You can revoke these permissions at any time in Android settings. OpenBlock will show that blocking stopped.",
  "restrictedSettingsTitle": "Is the switch greyed out?",
  "restrictedSettingsMessage": "On Android 13 and later, apps installed outside an app store must be allowed first: open App info, tap ⋮ and choose “Allow restricted settings”, then return to the accessibility settings.",
  "openAppInfo": "Open app info",
  "privacyLocalTitle": "Everything stays on this device",
  "privacyLocalBody": "Rules, settings, focus history and intervention counts are stored locally. OpenBlock has no account, no server and no analytics.",
  "privacyAccessibilityTitle": "Accessibility service",
  "privacyAccessibilityBody": "The service receives events about the app on screen. OpenBlock reads only the package name and, for feed rules in supported apps, whether elements with known identifiers are visible. It does not read or keep text, and it ignores apps without rules.",
  "privacyUsageTitle": "Usage access",
  "privacyUsageBody": "Usage minutes are read from Android only for apps that have rules, and only to enforce limits and show statistics.",
  "privacyNoNetworkTitle": "No network access",
  "privacyNoNetworkBody": "The app does not request the Internet permission, so it cannot send anything off the device.",
  "privacyDeleteTitle": "Deleting your data",
  "privacyDeleteBody": "Use Settings › Your data to delete statistics or everything. Uninstalling the app also removes all of its data.",
  "onboardingWelcomeTitle": "Take back your attention",
  "onboardingWelcomeBody": "OpenBlock helps you stop automatic scrolling and use apps on your own terms. You set the rules: block an app at certain hours, set a daily limit, block a feed such as YouTube Shorts where supported, or add a short pause before an app opens.\n\nNo account, no ads, no tracking.",
  "onboardingPermissionsTitle": "Permissions you grant",
  "onboardingPermissionsBody": "To act on other apps, Android requires permissions that only you can turn on in the system settings:\n\n• Accessibility service — notices which app is on screen and shows the pause or block screen over it. For feed rules it also checks whether a known feed is visible.\n\n• Usage access — reads how many minutes you used each app today, needed for daily limits.\n\nOpenBlock never turns these on by itself.",
  "onboardingDataTitle": "What OpenBlock can see",
  "onboardingDataBody": "• The package name of the app in the foreground.\n• In supported apps with a feed rule, the identifiers of on-screen elements, used only to recognise the feed.\n• Minutes of use per app, recorded by Android.\n\nIt does not read messages, passwords or what you type, and it does not store screen content. Nothing leaves your device.",
  "onboardingControlTitle": "You stay in control",
  "onboardingControlBody": "Pause or delete any rule, end a focus session at any time, or switch OpenBlock off completely:\n\n• Settings › Accessibility › OpenBlock › Off\n• Settings › Apps › Special app access › Usage access\n\nUninstalling OpenBlock removes all of its data.",
  "onboardingSetupTitle": "Set up permissions",
  "onboardingSetupBody": "Grant what you need now or later from Settings › Permissions. Without permissions the app still opens, but it cannot block anything.",
